                <pb facs="0864" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg768"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Straus.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-05-13"><hi rendition="#italic">May 13,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 118.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to ackowledge the receipt of your
                    confidential dispatch No. 73, of the 28th ultimo, containing an additional
                    report on the subject of the claims of American citizens against Turkey.</p>
                <p>Your action in the matter is approved by the Department, and the energy and
                    intelligence with which you are pressing for a settlement are commended.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
